How can friends fail without thread safety?
    It can fail due to the fact that multiple threads can read and write shared data. Race conditions

    Read-modify-write
        If two users were to send a request to the same user at the same time, when they are writing to the same HashMap incomingRequests for the key of the user,
        it can lead to one of the requests being overwritten

    Check-then-act
        If the receiving user doesn't have an item in incomingRequests both senders will try to create a new item overwriting one

    When writing to the file if any of the maps are modified mid write the data will either be inaccurate or will cause a 'ConcurrentModificationException'

How did I make this feature thread safe?
        Using write locks ensures that when any of the maps are being modified no other thread can access it for either reading or writing
        Using read locks ensures that when accessing data they are not currently being modified meaning that all the data is accurate
        ConcurrentHashMaps for built-in safety

    Read-modify-write and check-then-act
        Full operations are wrapped in a write lock (mostly) so all updates will complete fully and uninterrupted
    Writing to File
        only happens when the function has the write lock so no inaccuracies with the writing